From 3a35060ae40197ea7cf6eccd3053dde391bde0e8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bryan Hoban <bryan.hoban@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 20:45:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] big-fella: DCN 1.x's MPC background black in the output's
 colour space

dcn10_update_visual_confirm_color() programs the MPC background from
pipe_ctx->visual_confirm_color, which commit_planes_for_stream() only fills
when dc->debug.visual_confirm is on (dc_update_visual_confirm_color). So it's
zero. DCN 1.x blends after the output CSC, in the output's colour space,
where zero is black only for RGB; on a YCbCr link it's green. At 4K60 DCN 1.0
(Raven: Ryzen 5 3500U, Vega 8) splits a plane into two pipes, and the top one
blends per-pixel alpha against the background (dcn10_update_mpcc): wherever
the compositor's scene stays transparent (KWin clears to (0,0,0,0)), HDR at
4K60 as YCbCr 4:2:0 showed green on half the screen. kwin-big-fella worked
round it (kwin-big-fella-opaque-primary.patch: pixel blend mode None on the
bottom plane).

Without visual confirm, use black in the stream's output colour space:
Y 64, Cb/Cr 512 for DM's YCbCr outputs (all limited range but
2020_YCBCR_FULL), color_space_to_black_color for RGB. Not DC's YCbCr black
(BLACK_COLOR_FORMAT_YUV_CV, Cb/Cr 0x1f4, what dc_update_visual_confirm_color
uses for DCN < 2.0 when it runs): the output CSC makes black Cb/Cr 512.5, and
500 is a dim green-grey (a first try with it left the transparent frame's
chroma CRC different from opaque black's on ryzen-fella). DCN 2+ blends in
RGB before the output CSC, so it's left alone.

Tested on ryzen-fella with tools/dv-amd-crc/bg-crc-test (no compositor; a
full-screen ARGB8888 plane, Pre-multiplied, 2160p60 YCbCr 4:2:0): a fully
transparent frame's CRTC CRCs were b888/b888/c4c2 against opaque black's
9b83/9b83/5c03 before, and are 9b83/9b83/5c03 now. In RGB both were and are
6db3.

[Hades: from YBLOD 0.3.3 (dangerouslaser/libreelec-yblod 3b3a983f93,
linux-9924-big-fella-dcn10-black-bg.patch; big-fella 69c770c), as
linux-9957, with one case added: COLOR_SPACE_2020_RGB_LIMITEDRANGE, black
at 64. color_space_to_black_color() puts it with the full range RGB spaces
(0, below black), and it is what DM chooses for BT.2020 RGB in limited
range (HDR with "Broadcast RGB" limited). Read against Linux 7.3.1 with the
Hades series: the only other caller of dc_update_visual_confirm_color()
without the debug option is disable_dangling_plane(), for a plane that is
going away; the Dolby Vision tunnel stays on COLOR_SPACE_SRGB (any other
output colour space refuses it, amdgpu_dm_dvbridge_refused.c), whose black
is 0 as before, so its bytes do not change. The same background shows in
Hades wherever nothing opaque covers the CRTC on DCN 1.0 and 1.01 with a
YCbCr output (linux-9969 sends HDR at 4K50/60 as 4:2:0): Kodi's GUI plane
is transparent around a scaled video plane. The offsets of the output CSC
matrices of DC (output_csc_matrix, 13 bits) give the black that this picks,
to within half a code, for every YCbCr matrix; 0x1f4 is 12.5 codes off
(checked on the host).]
---
 .../amd/display/dc/hwss/dcn10/dcn10_hwseq.c   | 45 ++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 44 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/dc/hwss/dcn10/dcn10_hwseq.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/dc/hwss/dcn10/dcn10_hwseq.c
index 097e4ac..39d89a8 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/dc/hwss/dcn10/dcn10_hwseq.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/dc/hwss/dcn10/dcn10_hwseq.c
@@ -2936,9 +2936,52 @@ void dcn10_update_visual_confirm_color(struct dc *dc,
 		int mpcc_id)
 {
 	struct mpc *mpc = dc->res_pool->mpc;
+	struct tg_color bg_color = pipe_ctx->visual_confirm_color;
+
+	/*
+	 * big-fella: the MPC background is what a pixel with alpha shows over
+	 * where nothing is below it. Without visual confirm, commit_planes_for_stream
+	 * never fills visual_confirm_color (dc_update_visual_confirm_color runs
+	 * only with dc->debug.visual_confirm), so it's zero. DCN 1.x blends after
+	 * the output CSC (in the output's colour space), where zero is black only
+	 * for RGB: on a YCbCr link (HDR at 4K60 as 4:2:0) it's green, and at 4K60
+	 * DCN 1.0 splits the plane into two pipes, the top one blending per-pixel
+	 * alpha (dcn10_update_mpcc), so wherever the compositor left the scene
+	 * transparent half the screen was green (ryzen-fella, Raven). Use black in
+	 * the output's colour space. Not color_space_to_black_color's YCbCr black
+	 * (BLACK_COLOR_FORMAT_YUV_CV, Cb/Cr 0x1f4): the output CSC turns black into
+	 * Cb/Cr 512.5 (offsets 0x1004 at 13 bits), and 500 is a dim green-grey;
+	 * DM's YCbCr output colour spaces are all limited range (Y 64) but
+	 * 2020_YCBCR_FULL. Until linux-yblod 7.3-7 KWin worked round it
+	 * (kwin-big-fella-opaque-primary.patch, pixel blend mode None on the
+	 * bottom plane).
+	 */
+	if (!dc->debug.visual_confirm && dc->ctx->dce_version < DCN_VERSION_2_0 &&
+	    pipe_ctx->stream) {
+		switch (pipe_ctx->stream->output_color_space) {
+		case COLOR_SPACE_YCBCR601:
+		case COLOR_SPACE_YCBCR709:
+		case COLOR_SPACE_YCBCR601_LIMITED:
+		case COLOR_SPACE_YCBCR709_LIMITED:
+		case COLOR_SPACE_YCBCR709_BLACK:
+		case COLOR_SPACE_2020_YCBCR_LIMITED:
+			bg_color = (struct tg_color){ .color_r_cr = 0x200, .color_g_y = 0x40, .color_b_cb = 0x200 };
+			break;
+		case COLOR_SPACE_2020_YCBCR_FULL:
+			bg_color = (struct tg_color){ .color_r_cr = 0x200, .color_g_y = 0, .color_b_cb = 0x200 };
+			break;
+		case COLOR_SPACE_2020_RGB_LIMITEDRANGE:
+			/* Hades: color_space_to_black_color has it as full range (0) */
+			bg_color = (struct tg_color){ .color_r_cr = 0x40, .color_g_y = 0x40, .color_b_cb = 0x40 };
+			break;
+		default:
+			color_space_to_black_color(dc, pipe_ctx->stream->output_color_space, &bg_color);
+			break;
+		}
+	}
 
 	if (mpc->funcs->set_bg_color) {
-		mpc->funcs->set_bg_color(mpc, &(pipe_ctx->visual_confirm_color), mpcc_id);
+		mpc->funcs->set_bg_color(mpc, &bg_color, mpcc_id);
 	}
 }
 
